/Alt (Diagram summarizing REACH evaluation tracks with six colored sections labeled A to F. Each track details dataset types, prevalence tiers, and unit counts: Track A \(controlled spike-ins\), Track B \(synthetic stress\), Track C \(null controls\), Track D \(natural blood/CTC prevalence\), Track E \(label-noise robustness\), and Track F \(intra-lineage contrast\). Track A, B, and C show four prevalence tiers each; Track F shows three. Totals: 1,110 primary, 15 diagnostic, 1,125 units per method, 140 units in Track A subset. Tracks are color-coded and indicate unit purpose, prevalence, and robustness context.)
